@startuml
title CDN Peering Lifecycle

start

:Initiate CDN peering through resource sharing;
if (Resource registration trigger valid?) then (resources available / update required / traffic surge / established peering encapsulation required)
if (Is the resource new?) then (new resource)
:Register service information and assign new resource ID;
else (existing resource)
:Update existing resource information;
endif
if (Traffic surge or established peering encapsulation required?) then (traffic surge requires mediator supply of local resources)
:Supply available local resources and IDs to mediator;
elseif (Traffic surge or established peering encapsulation required?) then (established peering arrangement requires SR encapsulation)
:Encapsulate local and delegated external resource information in SR instance;
else (neither traffic surge nor established peering encapsulation is required)
endif
if (Resource failure reported?) then (resource failure reported)
:Remove failed resource service information and decrement resource ID counter;
else (no resource failure reported)
endif
if (Should peering be triggered by workload conditions?) then (expected or unexpected load increase causes inability to handle workload and flash crowd exists)
:Send initialization request to mediator to trigger peering;
if (Are user requests acceptable under provider policy?) then (service requirements acceptable under provider policy)
:Create negotiated relationship through a legal document, financial statement, or SLA, include service levels, storage requirements, transfer rate, service duration, penalties, other preconditions, and specify administration, coordination, and disband or re-arrangement interactions for interconnection;
:Obtain resource and access information from SR and policies from PR;
:Generate service requirements;
else (service requirements not acceptable under provider policy)
endif
:Pass service requirements to local Peering Agent;
:Receive service requirements;
if (Preexisting peering arrangements exist?) then (preexisting peering arrangements exist in a long-term scenario)
:Return preexisting peering arrangements;
:Perform resource discovery with peers;
repeat
:Re-evaluate service requirements and renegotiate;
repeat while (insufficient resources acquired) is (true)
:Establish peering arrangement;
:Configure CDN peering protocols and advertise CDN configuration information;
fork
:Exchange content availability and load information, redirect requests to optimal peer;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
fork again
:Deploy and administer functional policies through the Policy Repository;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
fork again
:Cooperate to execute common goals;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
fork again
:Exchange accounting information and perform billing;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
end fork
else (no preexisting peering arrangements exist)
:Carry out short-term negotiation with identified peering targets;
:Perform resource discovery with peers;
repeat
:Re-evaluate service requirements and renegotiate;
repeat while (insufficient resources acquired) is (true)
:Establish peering arrangement;
:Configure CDN peering protocols and advertise CDN configuration information;
fork
:Exchange content availability and load information, redirect requests to optimal peer;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
fork again
:Deploy and administer functional policies through the Policy Repository;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
fork again
:Cooperate to execute common goals;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
fork again
:Exchange accounting information and perform billing;
if (Termination condition holds for existing peering arrangement?) then (termination condition holds)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement within negotiated scope;
else (no termination condition holds)
endif
stop
end fork
endif
else (no workload condition requires peering trigger)
endif
stop
else (none of the service registration triggers apply)
endif
if (Should peering be triggered by workload conditions?) then (expected or unexpected load increase causes inability to handle workload and flash crowd exists)
else (no workload condition requires peering trigger)
endif
stop

@enduml